{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-remix"},{"type":"text","value":". Import the UI factory from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-remix/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook({ options, ...components })"},{"type":"text","value":" once at module scope. Your app calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppChat(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" in a Remix setup function. Render "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<ui.Chat chat={chat} />"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory needs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every tool name in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". It also needs an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":" entry for every interrupt id. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generic.fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional. Widgets go in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":", the same way Form and Table register components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each widget is a Remix setup function. Read props from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handle.props"},{"type":"text","value":". If a widget needs live chat, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChatContext(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" in setup."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server route matches the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-5.6"},{"type":"text","value":" on the OpenAI text adapter."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./recipes/index","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chat UI recipes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport {\n  createChatHook,\n  type LayoutProps,\n  type MessageProps,\n  type PartProps,\n  type ToolProps,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { clientEntry, type Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout(handle: Handle<LayoutProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Messages, Interrupts, Queue, Input } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <main>\n            <Messages />\n            <Interrupts />\n            <Queue />\n            <Input />\n          </main>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n    message(handle: Handle<MessageProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Parts } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <article>\n            <Parts />\n          </article>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    fallback(handle: Handle<PartProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => <span>{handle.props.part.type}</span>\n    },\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n      return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport const ChatScreen = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function ChatScreen(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createAppChat(handle)\n    return () => <ui.Chat chat={chat} />\n  },\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layout"},{"type":"text","value":" receives these components. Render them as tags, not as calls:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Messages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Interrupts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Queue"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Input"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":" to draw the composer. Until then, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Input"},{"type":"text","value":" renders nothing. Register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queue"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"components"},{"type":"text","value":" to draw pending sends. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item.cancelQueued()"},{"type":"text","value":" on a queue item to drop it. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"message"},{"type":"text","value":" receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Parts"},{"type":"text","value":". A tool with an approval receives prop "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type a component in its own file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handle.props"},{"type":"text","value":" of a tool file with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolProps"},{"type":"text","value":". Share the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" module that you pass to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatHook"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\nexport function getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n  return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part"},{"type":"text","value":" is already a text part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupt components use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>"},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.payload"},{"type":"text","value":" matches the definition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mapped components do not receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat"},{"type":"text","value":" as a prop. If a component needs live chat, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-chat-from-ui-usechatcontext-handle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read chat from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext(handle)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui"},{"type":"text","value":" kit in a child file. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" only under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.Chat"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.Provider"},{"type":"text","value":". Call it in setup, not in the render function."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ui } from './chat-ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\n\nfunction MessageCount(handle: Handle) {\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext(handle)\n  return () => <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAppChat(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" owns the state. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.useChatContext(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the instance you passed into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.Chat"},{"type":"text","value":". A call outside that tree throws."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interrupts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool approvals sit in the tool when you read the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":" prop. Put a component on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.tools"},{"type":"text","value":" to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interruptsComponents.generic"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ choosePlan, fallback }"},{"type":"text","value":". An unbound interrupt uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":". If the copy must differ, branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt.kind === 'unbound'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full map is on the "},{"type":"link","href":"./react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React page"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"client","text":"Client","level":2},{"id":"type-a-component-in-its-own-file","text":"Type a component in its own file","level":2},{"id":"read-chat-from-ui-usechatcontext-handle","text":"Read chat from ui.useChatContext(handle)","level":2},{"id":"interrupts","text":"Interrupts","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-remix`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-remix/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `createAppChat(handle)` in a Remix setup function. Render `<ui.Chat chat={chat} />`.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nEach widget is a Remix setup function. Read props from `handle.props`. If a widget needs live chat, call `useChatContext(handle)` in setup.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport {\n  createChatHook,\n  type LayoutProps,\n  type MessageProps,\n  type PartProps,\n  type ToolProps,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { clientEntry, type Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout(handle: Handle<LayoutProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Messages, Interrupts, Queue, Input } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <main>\n            <Messages />\n            <Interrupts />\n            <Queue />\n            <Input />\n          </main>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n    message(handle: Handle<MessageProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Parts } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <article>\n            <Parts />\n          </article>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    fallback(handle: Handle<PartProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => <span>{handle.props.part.type}</span>\n    },\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n      return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport const ChatScreen = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function ChatScreen(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createAppChat(handle)\n    return () => <ui.Chat chat={chat} />\n  },\n)\n```\n\n`layout` receives these components. Render them as tags, not as calls:\n\n- `Messages`\n- `Interrupts`\n- `Queue`\n- `Input`\n\nRegister `input` on `components` to draw the composer. Until then, `Input` renders nothing. Register `queue` on `components` to draw pending sends. Call `item.cancelQueued()` on a queue item to drop it. `message` receives `Parts`. A tool with an approval receives prop `interrupt`.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nType the `handle.props` of a tool file with `ToolProps`. Share the same `chatOptions` module that you pass to `createChatHook`.\n\n```tsx\nimport type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\nexport function getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n  return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. If a component needs live chat, call `ui.useChatContext(handle)`.\n\n## Read chat from `ui.useChatContext(handle)`\n\nImport the same `ui` kit in a child file. Call `ui.useChatContext(handle)` only under `ui.Chat` or `ui.Provider`. Call it in setup, not in the render function.\n\n```tsx\nimport { ui } from './chat-ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\n\nfunction MessageCount(handle: Handle) {\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext(handle)\n  return () => <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}\n```\n\n`createAppChat(handle)` owns the state. `ui.useChatContext(handle)` reads the instance you passed into `ui.Chat`. A call outside that tree throws.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read the `interrupt` prop. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. If the copy must differ, branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'`.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Remix Chat UI\nid: typed-headless-ui-remix\norder: 7\ndescription: \"Build a typed, headless Remix 3 chat UI with createChatHook. Widgets are Remix setup functions.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - createChatHook\n  - remix\n  - headless ui\n  - ToolProps\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ai-remix`. Import the UI factory from `@tanstack/ai-remix/ui`. Call `createChatHook({ options, ...components })` once at module scope. Your app calls `createAppChat(handle)` in a Remix setup function. Render `<ui.Chat chat={chat} />`.\n\nThe factory needs a `toolsComponents` entry for every tool name in `chatOptions`. It also needs an `interruptsComponents.generic` entry for every interrupt id. `generic.fallback` is optional. Widgets go in `components`, `partsComponents`, `toolsComponents`, and `interruptsComponents`, the same way Form and Table register components.\n\nEach widget is a Remix setup function. Read props from `handle.props`. If a widget needs live chat, call `useChatContext(handle)` in setup.\n\nThe server route matches the [React page](./react). Use `gpt-5.6` on the OpenAI text adapter.\n\nThe [chat UI recipes](./recipes/index) show the same option groups one at a time. The code there is React, and the shape carries over.\n\n## Client\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-remix'\nimport {\n  createChatHook,\n  type LayoutProps,\n  type MessageProps,\n  type PartProps,\n  type ToolProps,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { clientEntry, type Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { createAppChat, ui } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout(handle: Handle<LayoutProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Messages, Interrupts, Queue, Input } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <main>\n            <Messages />\n            <Interrupts />\n            <Queue />\n            <Input />\n          </main>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n    message(handle: Handle<MessageProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => {\n        const { Parts } = handle.props\n        return (\n          <article>\n            <Parts />\n          </article>\n        )\n      }\n    },\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    fallback(handle: Handle<PartProps<typeof chatOptions>>) {\n      return () => <span>{handle.props.part.type}</span>\n    },\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n      return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport const ChatScreen = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function ChatScreen(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createAppChat(handle)\n    return () => <ui.Chat chat={chat} />\n  },\n)\n```\n\n`layout` receives these components. Render them as tags, not as calls:\n\n- `Messages`\n- `Interrupts`\n- `Queue`\n- `Input`\n\nRegister `input` on `components` to draw the composer. Until then, `Input` renders nothing. Register `queue` on `components` to draw pending sends. Call `item.cancelQueued()` on a queue item to drop it. `message` receives `Parts`. A tool with an approval receives prop `interrupt`.\n\n## Type a component in its own file\n\nType the `handle.props` of a tool file with `ToolProps`. Share the same `chatOptions` module that you pass to `createChatHook`.\n\n```tsx\nimport type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-remix/ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\nimport { chatOptions } from './chat-options'\n\nexport function getWeather(handle: Handle<ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>>) {\n  return () => <strong>{handle.props.part.input?.city}</strong>\n}\n```\n\nPart components use `PartProps<typeof chatOptions, 'text'>`. Then `part` is already a text part.\n\nInterrupt components use `InterruptProps<typeof chatOptions, 'choosePlan'>`. Then `interrupt.payload` matches the definition.\n\nMapped components do not receive `chat` as a prop. If a component needs live chat, call `ui.useChatContext(handle)`.\n\n## Read chat from `ui.useChatContext(handle)`\n\nImport the same `ui` kit in a child file. Call `ui.useChatContext(handle)` only under `ui.Chat` or `ui.Provider`. Call it in setup, not in the render function.\n\n```tsx\nimport { ui } from './chat-ui'\nimport type { Handle } from 'remix/ui'\n\nfunction MessageCount(handle: Handle) {\n  const chat = ui.useChatContext(handle)\n  return () => <p>{chat.messages.length} messages</p>\n}\n```\n\n`createAppChat(handle)` owns the state. `ui.useChatContext(handle)` reads the instance you passed into `ui.Chat`. A call outside that tree throws.\n\n## Interrupts\n\nTool approvals sit in the tool when you read the `interrupt` prop. Put a component on `interruptsComponents.tools` to send that approval to the list instead. Generic interrupts always sit in the list under `interruptsComponents.generic`: `{ choosePlan, fallback }`. An unbound interrupt uses `fallback`. If the copy must differ, branch on `interrupt.kind === 'unbound'`.\n\nThe full map is on the [React page](./react).\n"}
